{"id":"6a0df4ee-8830-4b1c-8fc2-31906e2623ef","revision":0,"last_node_id":32,"last_link_id":66,"nodes":[{"id":13,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-4170,-340],"size":[559.96875,1030.296875],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"READ ME FIRST","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## How to make a picture\n\n1. In the **green box (STEP 4)** type what you want to see. Plain sentences are fine.\n2. Press the blue **Run** button, top right.\n3. Wait 15-60 seconds. The picture(s) show up in **STEP 9**.\n\nEvery picture is archived automatically to `comfyui/output/freedom_archive/`, so\nnothing you make is ever lost. STEP 9 is where you send the *keepers* somewhere of\nyour own: click **Save Image** for a single picture, or tick the ones you want and\nclick **Save Selected Images**. **Set User Save Folder**, the button under Save\nImage, chooses where those copies go.\n\nThat's it. Everything else is already set up.\n\n### If you want to change something\n- **Different look / model:** click the file name in STEP 1.\n- **Her face on or off:** the **FACE ON / FACE OFF** button on STEP 2. Switched off,\n  the same picture is painted with a generic person instead, and the card you picked\n  is remembered for when you switch back.\n- **Add-on LoRAs:** STEP 3 starts with three rows and grows to twelve with\n  **+ Add LoRA**. Tick a row on, pick from the dropdown, set how strong it is - it\n  only lists LoRAs that actually match this checkpoint, so nothing you pick can be\n  the wrong architecture. (Emotions, expression\\_helper and Hands zib are NOT SDXL -\n  they are Flux / Krea / Z-Image LoRAs and will not appear here or work with\n  bigLust or Pony. This note used to say otherwise; that was wrong.)\n- **Wider or taller:** change the numbers in STEP 6.\n- **New random picture, same idea:** just press Run again.\n- **Keep the same picture, tweak wording:** on **STEP 7** set *control_after_generate*\n  to `fixed`, change a few words, Run."],"color":"#322","bgcolor":"#533"},{"id":14,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-3480,-300],"size":[559.921875,267.34375],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"STEP 1 - the art model","properties":{},"widgets_values":["**STEP 1 - the art model**\n\nThis opens the 'brain' that knows how to paint - **bigLust**, a photo-real model made for adult images.\n\nIt feeds three things to the rest of the recipe: the painter, the part that reads your words, and the part that turns the result into a normal picture.\n\n**You touch this only** to switch models - click the file name to pick lustify, CyberRealistic Pony, etc."],"color":"#233","bgcolor":"#355"},{"id":1,"type":"CheckpointLoaderSimple","pos":[-3480,30],"size":[559.921875,109.921875],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"ckpt_name","name":"ckpt_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"ckpt_name"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"MODEL","name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[43]},{"localized_name":"CLIP","name":"CLIP","type":"CLIP","links":[44]},{"localized_name":"VAE","name":"VAE","type":"VAE","links":[41]}],"title":"STEP 1  -  Pick the art model","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"CheckpointLoaderSimple","cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.33.0","models":[{"name":"sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors","url":"https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0/resolve/main/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors?download=true","directory":"checkpoints"}]},"widgets_values":["cyberrealisticPony_v110.safetensors"]},{"id":24,"type":"FreedomFaceSource","pos":[-3420,250],"size":[419.921875,109.953125],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"mode","name":"mode","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"mode"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"mode","name":"mode","type":"COMBO","slot_index":0,"links":[58]},{"localized_name":"mode_text","name":"mode_text","type":"STRING","slot_index":1,"links":[57]}],"title":"STEP 2  -  Face source switch (trained / random / off)","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"FreedomFaceSource"},"widgets_values":["trained_face"]},{"id":22,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-2790,-300],"size":[899.984375,753.09375],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"STEP 3 - pick her face","properties":{},"widgets_values":["**Pick her face**\n\nThis is the shelf of every face you've trained. Click a picture to put that person's face - or face and body - onto whatever gets painted below. Each trained person shows up as two cards: one for face-only, one for face + body.\n\n**The FACE ON / FACE OFF switch.** At the top of the shelf is a button that reads **FACE ON** in green. It decides whether this whole step does anything at all. Click it once and it turns red and reads **FACE OFF**.\n\n**What FACE OFF really means.** The picture gets painted exactly as if this step were not in the workflow at all. Her face is not applied, and her trigger word is left out of your prompt as well. (A trigger word is the made-up word her training gave her, something like `br1tany woman`. It is the word that tells the art model to draw her and not a stranger.) So with the switch off, nothing about her reaches the picture - not her face, and not her name.\n\n**Your pick is not lost.** The card you clicked stays clicked, just greyed out, and switching back on brings her straight back at the same strength. That is the difference between this switch and the **None** button beside it: **None** forgets who you picked, while the switch only pauses her.\n\n**Two buttons, one switch.** You can flip it from the button on the shelf, or from the small toggle on the node itself just above the shelf, which reads **face ON** / **face OFF**. They are wired together, so moving either one moves both. You never have to wonder which one is in charge.\n\n**When to use it.** Turn her off to try a new prompt, a new pose, or a different art model on a generic person first, so her face isn't pulling the picture around while you experiment. Then turn her back on and make the real one.\n\nThe **strength** slider controls how strongly her face takes over - 0.9 is a good starting point. Lower it toward 0.7 if her face comes out stiff, raise it toward 1.0 if it doesn't look enough like her.\n\n**Refresh** picks up any face you've just finished training without restarting anything."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"FreedomFaceShelf","pos":[-2780,520],"size":[889.984375,731.1875],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":17,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"model","name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":43},{"localized_name":"clip","name":"clip","type":"CLIP","link":44},{"localized_name":"face_mode","name":"face_mode","shape":7,"type":"STRING","link":57},{"localized_name":"strength","name":"strength","type":"FLOAT","widget":{"name":"strength"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"selected","name":"selected","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"selected"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"enabled","name":"enabled","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"enabled"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"trigger_weight","name":"trigger_weight","type":"FLOAT","widget":{"name":"trigger_weight"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"model","name":"model","type":"MODEL","links":[45]},{"localized_name":"clip","name":"clip","type":"CLIP","links":[46]},{"localized_name":"trigger","name":"trigger","type":"STRING","links":[59]},{"localized_name":"person","name":"person","type":"STRING","links":[]}],"title":"STEP 3  -  Pick her face","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"FreedomFaceShelf"},"widgets_values":[0.9,"susana_head_body_sdxl_pony",true,1,""]},{"id":25,"type":"PortraitMasterBaseCharacter","pos":[-1230,1470],"size":[430,700],"flags":{"collapsed":true},"order":15,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"text_in","name":"text_in","shape":7,"type":"STRING","link":61},{"localized_name":"shot","name":"shot","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"shot"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"shot_weight","name":"shot_wei